 1.1 GiB across all 45 tasks before NPZ compression. Consolidated gzip search
 records, diagnostics, ledgers, and temporary restart checkpoints are expected
@@ -136,6 +136,16 @@ factor-Ridge, PLS, and gradient boosting also reuse one float32 row-history
 design per fold and lag group. Pooled and target Ridge reuse the corresponding
 full-lag design.
 
+The first `dev-2020` resource pilot measured about 11 minutes for factor Ridge
+and about 62 minutes for the former 180-trial CP grid. The expanded 360-trial
+CP grid should therefore be budgeted for at least two hours. The former
+256-trial Tucker grid finished in about 14 minutes, but the rank-aware output
+score filter and four-cap search require a fresh measurement. Gradient
+boosting completed 144 of 864 trials in about 3.3 hours, implying roughly
+20 hours at the observed pace. These are development-only pilot measurements,
+not task time limits; detached workers may run for days when the manifest
+remains scientifically admissible.
+
 The largest four-year inner-fold preparation retains approximately 1.1 GiB of
 float32 tensor payload before masks, targets, and temporary numerical-library
 workspace. Nested search therefore runs one structural trial group at a time
diff --git a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
index 6371049..de7a887 100644
--- a/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
+++ b/logs/RESEARCH_LOG.md
@@ -866,3 +866,37 @@
   a prespecified high-cap stability comparison; the minimum-valid threshold is
   unchanged. These remediations use resource/convergence evidence only, not
   outer tensor forecasts, economics, candidate data, or final-holdout data.
+- Audited the replacement development-only manifest
+  `taq5m-dev-v3-stagea-e3183f4`, bound to source commit
+  `e3183f4e600e2c923f5591b0d8b019269b976b17` and manifest SHA-256
+  `0ef1c72a9d94505fa63b8071095cf5e7b7daf0180623d924fa6464d5098814ff`.
+  Factor Ridge completed 72/72 trials with `OUTER_EVALUATED`; its selected
+  factor count was one, selected alpha was 10, and primary scaled pooled
+  outer R-squared was 0.5935346.
+- CP accounted for all 180 trials, with 150 valid and 30 failed configurations.
+  The selected rank was five at the upper search boundary, so the task
+  correctly returned `SEARCH_EXPANSION_REQUIRED` and did not open outer tensor
+  validation. The matched 500- and 1000-iteration configurations had identical
+  loss, seed loss coefficient of variation was 0.001642, and the selected
+  maximum spatial condition number was about 8,843. The CP rank grid is
+  therefore expanded through ranks 6, 8, 10, 12, and 16 while preserving all
+  prior ranks, regularization values, caps, initializations, seeds, folds, and
+  admission gates.
+- Tucker accounted for all 256 trials, with 64 valid and 192 failed
+  configurations, and correctly returned `INSUFFICIENT_VALID_TRIALS` without
+  opening outer tensor validation. The selected valid configuration had
+  input/output ranks 3/3 and maximum output-score Gram condition about
+  `1.38e20`. Early inner samples had as few as four observed output coordinates
+  for nine latent score dimensions, exposing an underidentified normal-equation
+  solve rather than an economic result. Tucker output scores now use
+  rank-aware least squares, exclude empty, underidentified, and over-threshold
+  training samples separately, and report every exclusion. The iteration-cap
+  grid is expanded to 250, 500, 1000, and 2000, yielding 512 declared
+  configurations while retaining the 100-valid-trial gate.
+- Gradient boosting was stopped through the project worker-control path after
+  144/864 checkpoints because the manifest was already scientifically
+  unapprovable, not because long runtime was disallowed. Its observed pace
+  implied roughly 20 hours for the full task. The corrected manifest will let
+  all four pilots run to terminal evidence even when that takes days. No
+  candidate or final-holdout data, tensor outer forecast, Stage B economic
+  result, or protected outcome informed these changes.
